 "reading": "Where the evidence is good the design effects are too small to reorder the organ ranking (tubulin ratio 0.29, rank corr 0.947), so the within-arm metric is the baseline's metric and the design terms only add noise. Where the effects are large the evidence is one drug (dna_alkyl ratio 0.71 on a single agent). A design coefficient is identified by agents, not patients, but the binomial likelihood counts patients, so a two-arm cell still carries hundreds of patients and the hierarchical prior does not shrink it enough.",
